1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,900
Once, according to a Chinese legend,

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:06,160
ten suns rose together instead of taking

3
00:00:06,160 --> 00:00:08,400
turns. Rivers dried,

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,300
crops burned, and ordinary people suffered under

5
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:13,457
relentless heat.

6
00:00:14,260 --> 00:00:16,480
The earth could not survive ten heavens

7
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:17,740
burning at once.

8
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:21,520
Hunters, farmers, and animals searched in vain

9
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:22,920
for water or shade.

10
00:00:23,577 --> 00:00:25,460
Hou Yi raised his bow.

11
00:00:26,060 --> 00:00:28,340
He was asked to restore balance where

12
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:31,060
power from above had scorched the world

13
00:00:31,060 --> 00:00:31,623
below.

14
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:34,280
He shot down nine suns,

15
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:35,480
one after another.

16
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:38,720
Each impact dimmed the sky until only

17
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:40,880
the light the world needed remained.

18
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:44,440
With a single sun moving overhead,

19
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:46,300
crops could grow again.

20
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:49,180
Water returned to land that had nearly

21
00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:50,120
become desert.

22
00:00:51,264 --> 00:00:53,580
The hero did not make the world

23
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:55,960
safe by destroying all power.

24
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:58,520
He made it livable by leaving enough

25
00:00:58,520 --> 00:00:59,440
and no more.
